[22.137732, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[34m$\u001b[0m  lex run --allow-effects fs_write,io,net,proc,sql,time \\\r\n"]
[22.751637, "o", "        examples/spec_gated_agent.lex main 2>&1 | fmt\r\n"]
[23.33175, "o", "lex-llm  ·  Spec-gated agent tools  Typed permissions · property-checked · formally verified  (zero LLM API calls — spec evaluator and tool filter are pure functions)  \r\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n  1 — The spec: order_submit_policy  \r\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n  IF tool == \"submit_order\"  THEN qty <= 1000 AND approved == true  (vacuously true for all other tool names)  \r\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n  2 — Spec evaluation: four tool-call scenarios  \r\n────────────────────────"]
[23.331827, "o", "──────────────────────────────────────\r\n  A  tool=submit_order  qty=100   approved=true\r\n    verdict:  Allow ✓  B  tool=submit_order  qty=5000  approved=true\r\n    verdict:  Deny ✗  — predicate false: ((tool == \"submit_order\") => ((qty <= 1000) and (approved == true)))  C  tool=submit_order  qty=100   approved=false\r\n    verdict:  Deny ✗  — predicate false: ((tool == \"submit_order\") => ((qty <= 1000) and (approved == true)))  D  tool=get_quote     qty=0     approved=false\r\n    verdict:  Allow ✓  \r\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n  3 — Property check: check_random(spec, 100, seed=42)  \r\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
[23.331852, "o", "\r\n\r\n  ✓  spec holds for 100 random inputs  \r\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n  4 — SMT-LIB export (paste into z3 to formally verify)  \r\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n; SMT-LIB 2 script generated by lex-spec for `order_submit_policy`\r\n; Asserts the negation of the predicate; `unsat` ⇒ spec holds.\r\n(set-logic ALL)\r\n(declare-const tool String)\r\n(declare-const qty Int)\r\n(declare-const approved Bool)\r\n(assert (not (=> (= tool \"submit_order\") (and (<= qty 1000) (= approved true)))))\r\n(check-sat)\r\n(get-model)\r\n  \r\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r"]
[23.331869, "o", "\r\n  5 — Tool availability filtering  \r\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n  Permission level: trading-desk  (approved=true, qty-context=100)\r\n  Available: 3/3 tools\r\n    • get_quote\r\n    • read_positions\r\n    • submit_order\r\n  Permission level: read-only     (approved=false)\r\n  Available: 2/3 tools\r\n    • get_quote\r\n    • read_positions  \r\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n"]
[23.334592, "o", "\r\n"]
[24.84283, "o", "\u001b[2m"]
[24.843248, "o", "────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32mDONE\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[24.843403, "o", "\r\n  The same spec that gates tool calls at runtime can be property-checked\r\n  and formally verified — without touching an LLM or a database.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[36meval\u001b[0m      three-valued verdict (Allow / Deny / Inconclusive) per call\r\n"]
[24.843462, "o", "  \u001b[36mcheck\u001b[0m     100 seeded random inputs, deterministic, no flakiness\r\n  \u001b[36msmt\u001b[0m       Z3-ready negation — paste into z3, get 'unsat' = proof\r\n"]
[24.843497, "o", "  \u001b[36mfilter\u001b[0m    trading-desk: 3/3 tools · read-only: 2/3 (submit_order gated)\r\n\r\n"]
[24.844175, "o", "\u001b[2m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
